# Netlib infeasible subset — NOT YET PINNED. See PLAN 2.8.2 and Q6.
#
# This set asks the one question the standard set cannot: given a model with
# no feasible point, does JAOS say so — and does it ever report an optimum
# for one? Nothing else in M1 tests that direction. It is not hypothetical:
# the revert of 2026-08-07 was forced by its mirror image, a feasible
# instance (pilot-we) being reported INFEASIBLE, and no test in the suite
# would have caught the reverse.
#
# Run with:  build/bench/run -m bench/netlib-infeas.manifest -e infeasible
#
# The runner is ready. The instances are not, and cannot be until Q6 is
# decided: netlib distributes this set at netlib.org/lp/infeas/ in packed
# emps form only (verified 2026-08-07 by fetching `galenet` and reading its
# header), Koch's plain-MPS mirror does not carry it, and expanding it needs
# either netlib's emps — third-party source, a D11 call for the maintainer —
# or a plain-MPS mirror worth pinning. Nobody has looked for the latter.
#
# Format is the standard manifest's, so one parser serves both:
#
#     name  sha256  rows  cols  reference  source  objconst
#
# `reference` and `objconst` are unused here and are written 0.0: the verdict
# IS the reference. `source` records where the instance came from. rows/cols
# still matter — a reader that dropped the very rows making a model
# infeasible would otherwise "pass" for exactly the wrong reason.
#
# The 29 instances, from netlib.org/lp/infeas/ (readme and changes are not
# instances):
#
#   bgdbg1   bgetam   bgindy   bgprtr   box1     ceria3d  chemcom
#   cplex1   cplex2   ex72a    ex73a    forest6  galenet  gosh
#   gran     greenbea itest2   itest6   klein1   klein2   klein3
#   mondou2  pang     pilot4i  qual     reactor  refinery vol1
#   woodinfe
#
# Note `greenbea` here is NOT the greenbea of the standard set; it is a
# different, infeasible model that happens to share the name. Whatever
# fetches this set must keep the two apart on disk.
